{{also|heart-burn}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|heart-burn}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hertbryne}}, {{m|enm|herte-bren|t=lust", also "heartburn|lit=heart burn}}, equivalent to {{com|en|heart|burn}}. Compare also {{cog|enm|herte-brennyng|t=anger, bitterness, heartburn|lit=burning of/in the heart, heart-burning}}. Compare also {{noncog|grc|καρδιαλγία}}, from {{m|grc|καρδία||heart}} + {{m|grc|ἄλγος||pain}}. From being a burning sensation near the location of the heart in the chest.

